  <name>Porthole</name>
  <summary>Use Windows PCs from your Linux desktop</summary>
  <developer id="io.github.vladgb">
    <name>Vlad Baesu</name>
  </developer>

  <description>
    <p>
      Porthole is a Remote Desktop (RDP) client. Connect to a Windows PC and use it as if you
      were sitting in front of it: the remote desktop follows the size of the window, your
      keyboard shortcuts go to the PC, and its sound plays here.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Keep your PCs in one place, with a picture of each one's last session</li>
      <li>Smooth H.264 video, or a lossless mode for sharp text and exact colours</li>
      <li>Full screen on one monitor or across all of them</li>
      <li>Copy and paste text, images and files between this computer and the PC</li>
      <li>Use your microphone and webcam in calls on the PC</li>
      <li>Open local folders on the PC as drives</li>
      <li>Passwords are kept in your keyring</li>
    </ul>
  </description>

  <launchable type="desktop-id">io.github.vladgb.Porthole.desktop</launchable>

